{
  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved only 52.7% validation accuracy at 0.85 GPU hours. With just one data point, the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality is actually contributing signal or adding noise. Question tested: config_045 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is a clean A/B comparison that removes only the image branch while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and architecture identical to config_001. If RNA-alone matches or exceeds 52.7%, the image modality is not helping and I should redirect remaining budget toward RNA encoder upgrades (scgpt, scvi_n200) and multiprofile aggregation. If RNA-alone is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed valuable and I should prioritize image encoder (ViT-L) and fusion strategy improvements. Why this is the best next experiment: it is extremely cheap (~0.3–0.5 GPU hours, RNA-only with PCA and no image processing), so it costs a small fraction of the budget while resolving the single most consequential design question—whether to invest remaining experiments in multimodal or unimodal architectures. This information will shape the strategy for all 8 remaining experiments far more effectively than a small incremental change (e.g., switching concat→weighted fusion) or a costly multimodal variant that conflates multiple variables."
}

